带有一种老派小镇的感觉。

00:46:09.760 --> 00:46:10.559
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.
对，对，对，对，对，对。

00:46:10.559 --> 00:46:13.920
He likes classical music too, classical literature too.
他也喜欢古典音乐，古典文学也喜欢。

00:46:13.920 --> 00:46:18.320
But I can't say that any one of us was a huge jazz guy, that that's why we put it in.
但我不能说我们当中有谁是个超级爵士乐迷，所以才把这个放进去。

00:46:18.320 --> 00:46:20.079
I feel it's more in the decor than.
我觉得这更多体现在布景装饰里。

00:46:20.079 --> 00:46:27.840
It might have been one of those reverse engineered things because I think they started putting me in like jazz t-shirts, like, do you know what I'm saying?
这可能是那种事后反向推导出来的东西，因为我觉得他们开始给我穿那种爵士乐T恤，呃，你知道我的意思吗？

00:46:27.840 --> 00:46:35.511
Like, I think they were, I think then you were like, I don't think we were writing it that way as much as like wardrobe and set deck or like this, Ted would like this.
就像，我觉得他们当时在做，而你会觉得，我们写剧本的时候可能没写那么多，反而是服装和布景部门觉得，泰德会喜欢这个。

00:46:35.511 --> 00:46:40.196
I think that might have been like a little bit and maybe then we decided to reference it a little bit.
我觉得这可能有点那种意思，然后也许我们决定在台词里稍微呼应一下。

00:46:40.196 --> 00:46:51.679
It's a very interesting like ecosystem where in all parts of the ecosystem kind of feed each other in some kind of cycle, like the, you know, wardrobe and set deck will do something and we'll go like, oh yeah, maybe we'll Maybe we'll talk about that.
这是一个非常有趣的生态系统，生态系统的各个部分在某种循环中相互滋养，比如，你知道的，服装和布景部门会做一些事，然后我们会说，哦，对，也许我们可以谈谈这个。

00:46:51.679 --> 00:46:52.519
It's not always for the writer.
这并不总是为了编剧而设的。

00:46:52.519 --> 00:47:03.400
Well, they're reading the script, like they're reading it through the lens of like what clothes were these people were wearing, what's on the walls, but they're also paying attention to the characters because all that stuff is character revealing.
嗯，他们在读剧本时，会从这些人在穿什么衣服、墙上有什么东西的角度去解读，但他们也会关注角色，因为所有这些东西都能揭示角色的性格。

00:47:03.400 --> 00:47:04.800
Yeah, exactly.
对，确实如此。

00:47:04.800 --> 00:47:07.159
And that's, yeah, I would give them the credit there.
而且，是的，我觉得这一点上他们值得表扬。

00:47:07.159 --> 00:47:12.360
I think that's much more from like the art design perspective of Ted than from the writing side.
我觉得这更多是出于泰德的美术设计视角，而不是编剧层面。

00:47:12.360 --> 00:47:14.639
If you have questions, just check us on Instagram.
如果你有任何问题，可以在Instagram上关注我们。

00:47:14.639 --> 00:47:18.480
It's a great way to send in your questions as well as through the website, as Josh had mentioned.
正如乔希所提到的，这也是发送你的问题以及通过网站联系我们的好方法。

00:47:18.480 --> 00:47:24.119
And another great thing to send in through the website are these letters that we read and we have a lovely one today, Josh?
通过网站发来的另一个好东西就是我们读的这些信件，我们今天有一封很棒的信，乔希？

00:47:24.119 --> 00:47:24.619
Yeah.
对。

00:47:24.619 --> 00:47:26.701
So this one is from Sarah.
所以这封信来自莎拉。

00:47:26.701 --> 00:47:27.421
Hi, guys.
大家好。

00:47:27.421 --> 00:47:34.306
I'm one of those millennials now in my 30s who saw this on TV when I was really young.
我是那种三十多岁的千禧一代，我很小的时候就在电视上看过这部剧。

00:47:34.306 --> 00:47:38.949
Then during uni, watched it as it blew up with my friends.
后来在大学期间，看着它和朋友们一起火了起来。

00:47:38.849 --> 00:47:54.130
My partner at the time spoke so highly of this show because in his words, it was realistic as in so great to see a show where people hung out at bars and not coffee places, lived in tiny flats and struggled with life rather than pretending to struggle.
我当时的伴侣对这部剧评价很高，因为用他的话说，它很现实，能看到一部剧里的人是在酒吧而不是咖啡馆闲逛，住在狭小的公寓里，为生活挣扎而不是假装挣扎，这太棒了。

00:47:54.130 --> 00:47:58.650
Years on, I remain perpetually single and I watch him yum every year.
多年以后，我依然单身，每年都会重温这部剧。

00:47:58.650 --> 00:48:01.650
Not intentionally, it's just comfort food for me.
倒不是故意为之，它只是我的精神慰藉。

00:48:01.650 --> 00:48:05.909
For some reason, I always start with the Christmas episode where Lily is a Grinch.
不知为何，我总是从莉莉当格林奇的那集圣诞节开始看。

00:48:05.909 --> 00:48:21.329
Every time I watch for fun, every time I get drawn in and every time I ball my eyes out nearly every episode of the last season, because the romantic in me, who at this point is very cynical about life, still has a glimmer of hope that whoever it is I'm supposed to meet is just around the corner.
每次我为了好玩而看，每次都会被吸引进去，而且最后一季几乎每一集我都会哭得稀里哗啦，因为我内心深处那个浪漫主义者——尽管此时对生活已经非常愤世嫉俗——依然怀有一丝希望，觉得我命中注定要遇到的人就在拐角处。

00:48:21.329 --> 00:48:23.130
I am very much a Ted.
我真的很像泰德。

00:48:23.130 --> 00:48:27.210
Like a lot of people are saying, HSP, highly sensitive person, hard on sleep.
就像很多人说的那样，HSP（高敏感人群），睡眠质量差。

00:48:27.210 --> 00:48:33.769
And at this point in my life, I super relate to the single fatigue Ted has towards the end of the show.
在我人生的这个阶段，我极其感同身受泰德在剧集快结束时那种单身的疲惫感。

00:48:33.769 --> 00:48:36.050
That'd be a good episode title, single fatigue.
这会是一个很好的剧集标题，单身疲惫。

00:48:36.050 --> 00:48:42.849
But enough of that misery, genuinely, I always end up bawling not out of sadness, but hope.
不过那些悲伤就说到这里，说实话，我最后总是泪流满面，不是因为难过，而是因为希望。

00:48:42.849 --> 00:48:50.769
And also just gratefulness that I am who I am and that I can feel this way and therefore experience life to its very fullest.
还有感激，感激我是现在的我，感激我有这种感受，从而能够体验最完整的人生。

00:48:50.769 --> 00:48:59.690
I really get a lot of lessons out of the show every time I watch, and I'm really grateful for the reminder that there's always an older me who will see things differently in retrospect.
每次看这部剧，我真的都能学到很多东西，并且我很感激它提醒了我：回首过去时，总有一个更成熟的我会有不同的看法。

00:48:59.690 --> 00:49:14.010
When I'm feeling particularly blue about my bad luck and love, I often think about how there's some plonker out there who hasn't met anyone like me yet, and I've not met anyone like them yet, and that makes me go giddy in the moment.
当我因为在爱情中运气不佳而感到格外沮丧时，我经常会想，外面一定有个笨蛋还没遇到过像我这样的人，而我也还没遇到过像他们那样的人，这让我当下感到一阵眩晕般的兴奋。

00:49:14.010 --> 00:49:17.210
How are we spelling plonker?
“笨蛋”（plonker）这个词怎么拼？

00:49:17.210 --> 00:49:18.050
Can you use, can you?
你能用一下吗，你可以吗？

00:49:18.050 --> 00:49:19.849
Oh, and K-E-R.
哦，还有 K-E-R。

00:49:19.849 --> 00:49:21.809
I love this word so much, plonker.
我太喜欢这个词了，笨蛋（plonker）。

00:49:21.809 --> 00:49:22.929
And that's her dream.
这就是她的梦想。

00:49:22.929 --> 00:49:24.090
I want to be the plonker.
我想当那个笨蛋。

00:49:24.090 --> 00:49:24.929
Yeah.
对。

00:49:24.929 --> 00:49:27.809
Some plonker out there who hasn't met anyone like me yet.
外面的某个笨蛋还没遇到过像我这样的人。

00:49:27.809 --> 00:49:29.690
And I've never met anyone like them yet.
而我也还没遇到过像他们那样的人。

00:49:29.690 --> 00:49:31.530
And that makes me go giddy in the moment.
这让我此刻感到眩晕。

00:49:31.530 --> 00:49:33.769
Thank you entirely for this.
非常感谢你们带来这一切。

00:49:33.769 --> 00:49:36.329
With love, Sarah.
爱你的，莎拉。

00:49:36.329 --> 00:49:39.449
Sarah, Sarah, may you meet your plonker?
莎拉，莎拉，愿你能遇到你的那个笨蛋！

00:49:40.409 --> 00:49:41.570
How I met my plonker.
老爸老妈的浪漫史（How I met my plonker）。

00:49:41.570 --> 00:49:44.309
When in just the right time.
在恰当的时候。

00:49:44.309 --> 00:49:51.929
I also, I also we've talked about this, but I hear when I hear from women who relate to Ted so much, I always find it comes up a lot, right?
我也，我们讨论过这个，但当我听到那些对泰德非常有共鸣的女性的心声时，我总是发现这种情况经常出现，对吧？

00:49:51.929 --> 00:49:53.805
I was thinking the exact same thing.
我刚才也在想完全一样的事情。

00:49:53.805 --> 00:49:54.795
We hear that a lot.
我们经常听到这种反馈。

00:49:54.795 --> 00:49:55.889
I think that's great.
我觉得这太棒了。

00:49:55.889 --> 00:49:56.389
Yeah.
对。

00:49:56.389 --> 00:49:58.629
Well, Sarah, thanks for that lovely letter.
好吧，莎拉，谢谢你写来这封可爱的信。

00:49:58.389 --> 00:50:05.590
We're wishing you all the best and we're glad we can accompany you through this strange journey called life.
我们祝你一切都好，也高兴能陪伴你走过这段被称为人生的奇妙旅程。

00:50:05.590 --> 00:50:13.710
I love that I love that the show has made it around the world in the way it has and we're hearing we started this episode with learning English and we ended the episode in England, I think.
我很高兴这部剧能以这种方式火遍全球，我觉得我们这集节目开始于学习英语，而结束于英国。

00:50:13.710 --> 00:50:16.710
It's really- And we learned something cool.
这真的是——而且我们学到了一些酷炫的知识。

00:50:16.710 --> 00:50:17.710
And we learned something cool.
而且我们学到了一些酷炫的知识。

00:50:17.710 --> 00:50:20.710
We've been some real, some Plankarisms.
我们了解了一些真正的英国俚语。

00:50:20.710 --> 00:50:23.710
Well, to all you Plankars out there, thank you for joining us.
好吧，所有的笨蛋们，谢谢你们加入我们。

00:50:23.710 --> 00:50:26.710
We loved being with you and we'll see you next time.
我们很享受和你们在一起的时光，我们下次再见。

